  "guide": {
    "title": "Follow a request through Hono",
    "introduction": {
      "text": "A request enters through fetch. Hono matches its route, runs the selected handlers, and chooses a response. A handler is a function that processes the request.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "claim:be525e2a-9f68-4196-b67c-7bf670fbee39",
        "claim:8b0483bd-c519-497b-b081-d286863646b7",
        "claim:3c7751cc-3137-4636-a809-aa2a0ee43c9e",
        "claim:2639197b-bb38-4ed2-9817-07e369a77759",
        "claim:7ce9d699-11e2-481a-866e-c1e4356ea24d"
      ],
      "unknown_indices": []
    },
    "example": {
      "title": "Start with one direct response",
      "description": {
        "text": "Assume the router finds exactly one handler. If that handler returns a Response directly, Hono returns it. No middleware composition is needed for this case.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "claim:3c7751cc-3137-4636-a809-aa2a0ee43c9e",
          "claim:abe1d0e6-876f-40a3-b8e1-aac696dd56f5"
        ],
        "unknown_indices": []
      }
    },
    "sections": [
      {
        "key": "route",
        "title": "First, match the request",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
            "text": "For a request other than HEAD, Hono resolves the path and asks the router for matching handlers.",
            "claim_ids": [
              "claim:889f741d-3df0-47f5-9e19-2a06a2a99445",
              "claim:8b0483bd-c519-497b-b081-d286863646b7"
            ],
            "unknown_indices": []
          },
          {
            "text": "It then creates a Context. This object carries the request, match result, environment, and response state through the selected path.",
            "claim_ids": [
              "claim:6ea34fc3-66d3-437b-a99c-f67c5043f6b6",
              "claim:6f5292fe-ce44-4891-9436-47ae3462ead0",
              "claim:1d2eae5b-efd0-4237-8671-50d5055dafe0"
            ],
            "unknown_indices": []
          },
          {
            "text": "HEAD is a special case: Hono dispatches with GET as the method argument, keeps the original Request, and creates a response without a body.",
            "claim_ids": [
              "claim:085248c3-81b0-4cad-986d-05fee44fe506",
              "claim:f30ea83a-a386-4f3c-93af-21067f7f47cb"
            ],
            "unknown_indices": []
          }
        ],
        "stage_keys": [
          "method",
          "match"
        ],
        "code": {
          "evidence_id": "evidence:98377407be0e1d9f3dbe99143801820905c18a26f23561c9fcf9d38afe55dcd2",
          "start_line": 420,
          "end_line": 429
        }
      },
      {
        "key": "handlers",
        "title": "Then, choose how to run the handlers",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
            "text": "Exactly one handler uses the direct path. Hono calls it with the context and a next callback.",
            "claim_ids": [
              "claim:3c7751cc-3137-4636-a809-aa2a0ee43c9e",
              "claim:d4c7dc38-cdfc-4a47-b9f5-c3628df16210"
            ],
            "unknown_indices": []
          },
          {
            "text": "Zero or multiple handlers use compose. Hono passes the matching middleware and configured error and not-found handlers, then waits for the composed runner.",
            "claim_ids": [
              "claim:2639197b-bb38-4ed2-9817-07e369a77759",
              "claim:c3467e33-ffa9-47f6-8a0f-934dcdd6024c",
              "claim:f551142e-2ef8-4131-9da8-304f6a92329e"
            ],
            "unknown_indices": []
          },
          {
            "text": "This choice matters when a handler does not return a response. The two paths use different rules.",
            "claim_ids": [
              "claim:876a95e6-ca91-46c2-b831-60091068b69d",
              "claim:abe1d0e6-876f-40a3-b8e1-aac696dd56f5",
              "claim:b962178a-0e5d-4e27-a698-38b48e7fdd3a"
            ],
            "unknown_indices": []
          }
        ],
        "stage_keys": [
          "handlers"
        ],
        "code": {
          "evidence_id": "evidence:98377407be0e1d9f3dbe99143801820905c18a26f23561c9fcf9d38afe55dcd2",
          "start_line": 431,
          "end_line": 450
        }
      },
      {
        "key": "response",
        "title": "Now, select the response",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
            "text": "The direct path first checks whether the returned value is a Promise.",
            "claim_ids": [
              "claim:3ebf7dad-d613-4994-9e9e-f59bb1d79317"
            ],
            "unknown_indices": []
          },
          {
            "text": "For a non-Promise result, null or undefined triggers the not-found handler. This branch does not check c.finalized.",
            "claim_ids": [
              "claim:abe1d0e6-876f-40a3-b8e1-aac696dd56f5"
            ],
            "unknown_indices": []
          },
          {
            "text": "For a Promise, a truthy resolved value wins. Otherwise, Hono uses c.res if c.finalized is true. If it is false, Hono calls the not-found handler.",
            "claim_ids": [
              "claim:32832fda-23d3-411c-8392-6782b3634057",
              "claim:876a95e6-ca91-46c2-b831-60091068b69d"
            ],
            "unknown_indices": []
          },
          {
            "text": "After composition, Hono requires a finalized context and returns context.res. An unfinalized context causes an Error.",
            "claim_ids": [
              "claim:b962178a-0e5d-4e27-a698-38b48e7fdd3a",
              "claim:7ce9d699-11e2-481a-866e-c1e4356ea24d"
            ],
            "unknown_indices": []
          },
          {
            "text": "The res getter does not finalize the context. The setter sets finalized to true, even when its argument is undefined.",
            "claim_ids": [
              "claim:161b91b9-a49b-44d3-a919-0758464c5af3",
              "claim:1d2eae5b-efd0-4237-8671-50d5055dafe0"
            ],
            "unknown_indices": []
          }
        ],
        "stage_keys": [
          "response"
        ],
        "code": {
          "evidence_id": "evidence:98377407be0e1d9f3dbe99143801820905c18a26f23561c9fcf9d38afe55dcd2",
          "start_line": 442,
          "end_line": 449
        }
      },
      {
        "key": "failure",
        "title": "Finally, follow any failure to its handler",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
            "text": "The direct handler catch, Promise rejection handler, and composition catch call #handleError. It delegates Error instances to the configured callback and rethrows other values.",
            "claim_ids": [
              "claim:3a465dfd-a823-4297-a867-dc7b31edd393",
              "claim:6b5a8b30-ea42-46e9-880d-53099dbe6c56",
              "claim:7af68846-ae57-44cd-8e06-49e5596a226b",
              "claim:f5f65ad6-ca98-41d8-95dd-293ac83d5f15"
            ],
            "unknown_indices": []
          },
          {
            "text": "The direct not-found fallback is outside the direct handler catch block. If it throws synchronously, that failure can reach the caller.",
            "claim_ids": [
              "claim:bf2950af-c55d-401a-9691-50acf819a3f2"
            ],
            "unknown_indices": []
          },
          {
            "text": "The default not-found handler uses status 404. The default error handler can use getResponse; otherwise, it logs the error and uses status 500.",
            "claim_ids": [
              "claim:4a289f87-40be-45fa-90f8-f07a20dcafb8",
              "claim:4e81a050-0232-49a7-bf88-ebfbdc1e9576",
              "claim:75a7f499-e2f0-4998-89a5-48c6456d3bab"
            ],
            "unknown_indices": []
          }
        ],
        "stage_keys": [
          "failure"
        ],
        "code": {
          "evidence_id": "evidence:d19ca748f1302f0092f3bbbc30148d3c2d835f99f407db8e27802045d7c85b69",
          "start_line": 401,
          "end_line": 406
        }
      }
    ],
    "limits": [
      {
        "text": "Your routes and application functions determine the actual behavior. Their implementation is outside these excerpts.",
        "claim_ids": [],
        "unknown_indices": [
          0
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Some failures leave this part of Hono. The excerpts do not show how the caller handles them.",
        "claim_ids": [],
